From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Il tuo nome <tu@esempio.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:21:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell, cpu/intel/haswell: Shorter help texts of
 four options

The CFR record of the ThinkPad W541 reached 28.5 KiB with the options
of v1.6.1, near the 32 KiB of the coreboot table that it shares with
the other records. Shorten the help texts of Hyper-Threading, the
internal microphone and the camera, which said more than the setup
needs, to keep about half a KiB free.

TEST=tools/cfr-dump.sh of ouroBIOS on the W541 build: 28132 bytes.

Change-Id: I75c64faf74c6c56f056fe37e4c8a2ef5c1dd9d15
---
 src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h        |  6 ++----
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c | 16 ++++++----------
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h
index 09b2d331e5..b732b117e0 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/cfr.h
@@ -108,10 +108,8 @@ static void update_hyper_threading(struct sm_object *new)
 static const struct sm_object hyper_threading = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.opt_name	= "hyper_threading",
 	.ui_name	= "Hyper-Threading",
-	.ui_helptext	= "Two threads per core. A change applies through a reset,\n"
-			  "which the firmware does by itself; while it is off, every\n"
-			  "power-on has that reset too, the OS sees one thread per\n"
-			  "core, and a resume from sleep keeps what the OS had.\n"
+	.ui_helptext	= "Two threads per core. A change applies through a reset the\n"
+			  "firmware does itself; while off, every power-on has it too.\n"
 			  "Default: on. Not listed on the processors without it.",
 	.default_value	= true,
 }, WITH_CALLBACK(update_hyper_threading));
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index 3a817240be..4756ebe2ea 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -324,11 +324,8 @@ static const struct sm_object internal_mic = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.opt_name	= "internal_mic",
 	.ui_name	= "Internal microphone",
 	.ui_helptext	= "The microphone array in the lid.\n"
-			  "Default: on. Off: the firmware tells the operating system\n"
-			  "that the microphone is not connected, so it is not offered\n"
-			  "as an input. A soft switch: the audio chip itself stays\n"
-			  "powered, and an OS that ignores the firmware's pin setup\n"
-			  "could still use it. The headset jack is not affected.",
+			  "Default: on. Off: reported to the OS as not connected (a\n"
+			  "soft switch). The headset jack is not affected.",
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
 
@@ -734,11 +731,10 @@ static const struct sm_object camera = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.flags		= CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
 	.opt_name	= "camera",
 	.ui_name	= "Integrated camera",
-	.ui_helptext	= "The camera above the display, a USB device of the chipset.\n"
-			  "Default: on. Off: its USB port is disabled in the USB 3.0\n"
-			  "controller at every start and wake, so no OS sees the\n"
-			  "camera. An OS that routes the port to the USB 2.0\n"
-			  "controller instead would still find it.",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The camera above the display.\n"
+			  "Default: on. Off: its USB port is disabled at every start\n"
+			  "and wake (an OS routing it to the USB 2.0 controller would\n"
+			  "still find it).",
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
 
-- 
